==German==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh}} {{m|gmh|klette}}, from {{etyl|goh}} {{m|goh|kletta|g=f}}, {{m|goh|kletto|g=m}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*gleyt-||to cling to, cleave, stick}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*gley-}}. Cognate with {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|kledda|g=f}}, {{m|osx|kleddo|g=m}} and {{etyl|gml|-}} {{m|gml|klette}}. Related to {{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|klettern||to climb}} and {{m|de|Kleid||dress}}, also {{etyl|dum|-}} {{m|dum|clisse}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|klis}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|cliþe}}, {{m|ang|clāte}} and {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|clote||burdock}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈklɛtə/|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|ɛtə|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Kletten}}
# [[burdock]]
# a [[burr]] (a seed pod with sharp features that stick in fur or clothing)
# {{label|de|figuratively}} a clingy person

